.TH "WEBTRANSPORTSENDGROUP.GETSTATS" "3JS" "September 1, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
WebTransportSendGroup.getStats \- WebTransportSendGroup: getStats()
method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]getStats()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]WebTransportSendGroup\f[R] interface returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R]
that resolves to an object containing statistics aggregated across all
of the \f[CR]WebTransportSendStream\f[R] objects currently associated
with this group.
That is, every stream whose \f[CR]sendGroup\f[R] is set to this
\f[CR]WebTransportSendGroup\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
getStats()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves to an object containing aggregated
statistics for the group\(cqs streams.
The returned object has the following properties:
.TP
\f[B]bytesAcknowledged\f[R]
A non\-negative integer indicating the number of bytes written to the
group\(cqs streams that have been sent and acknowledged as received by
the server, using QUIC\(cqs ACK mechanism.
Only sequential bytes up to, but not including, the first unacknowledged
byte of each stream, are counted.
This number can only increase and is always less than or equal to
\f[CR]bytesSent\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]bytesSent\f[R]
A non\-negative integer indicating the number of bytes written to the
group\(cqs streams that have been sent at least once (but not
necessarily acknowledged).
This number can only increase, and is always less than or equal to
\f[CR]bytesWritten\f[R].
Note that this count does not include bytes sent as network overhead
(such as packet headers).
.TP
\f[B]bytesWritten\f[R]
A non\-negative integer indicating the number of bytes successfully
written to the group\(cqs streams.
This number can only increase.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
The code snippet below uses \f[CR]await\f[R] to wait on the
\f[CR]Promise\f[R] returned by \f[CR]getStats()\f[R], then logs the
number of bytes that have been sent across the group\(cqs streams but
not yet acknowledged:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] stats = \f[B]await\f[R] sendGroup.getStats();
\f[B]const\f[R] bytesNotAcknowledged = stats.bytesSent \- stats.bytesAcknowledged;
console.log(\(gaBytes sent but not yet acknowledged: ${bytesNotAcknowledged}\(ga);
.EE
